A woman in her sixties waved me over to her stall. Her face was weathered but kind, illuminated by the warm glow of a single hanging bulb. She placed a bowl in front of me—Bún chả. The grilled pork was caramelized and smoky, the noodles fresh, the herbs fragrant.

